    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Ben Pennell",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I see two references to it<br/>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-kernel-modeshape/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/kernel/modeshape/rdf/impl/AclRdfContext.java#L57\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-kernel-modeshape/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/kernel/modeshape/rdf/impl/AclRdfContext.java#L57</a><br/>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-http-commons/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/http/commons/responses/ViewHelpers.java#L202\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-http-commons/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/http/commons/responses/ViewHelpers.java#L202</a></p>\n\n<p>Apparently `fedora:writable` controls if the “Update Content” panel appears in the html ui.</p>\n\n<p>It also appears to be telling us if modeshape is giving any of the following permissions “add_node,set_property,remove”. That seems a little out dated given that we are not relying on modeshape permissions anymore. I’m not sure if others feel that it is still necessary to provide a triple that tells the user if they can write to a resource, but the current implementation is inaccurate. We will probably need to update how the “Update Content” panel gets rendered too if I’m reading things correctly (edited)</p>",
     "created": "12/Nov/18 6:04 PM",
     "id": "20522",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/12824/comment/20522",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Ben Pennell",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "12/Nov/18 6:04 PM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/be7c7dc994e3e4d444fe0c6473628654?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPE-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/be7c7dc994e3e4d444fe0c6473628654?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPE-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/be7c7dc994e3e4d444fe0c6473628654?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPE-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/be7c7dc994e3e4d444fe0c6473628654?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPE-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Peter Matthew Eichman",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>My feeling is that we should figure out a way to fix <tt>fedora:writable</tt> so a client application or a user can know in advance if they can write to a resource. Also, with the support of <tt>acl:Appends</tt> mode in WebAC, should we think about adding a <tt>fedora:appendable</tt> triple as well, to differentiate these two use cases?</p>\n\n<p>As an alternative, if there was a way for the resource to return an HTTP header that indicates what modes the requesting user has permission on the current resource, that would help. Something like this for read-only access:</p>\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>Access-Mode: &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#Read&gt; </pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>read/append (but not write):</p>\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>Access-Mode: &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#Read&gt;,\r\n    &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#Append&gt;</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>read/append/write (but not control):</p>\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>Access-Mode: &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#Read&gt;,\r\n    &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#Append&gt;,\r\n    &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#Write&gt;</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>all modes:</p>\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>Access-Mode: &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#Read&gt;,\r\n    &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#Append&gt;,\r\n    &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#Write&gt;,\r\n    &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#Control&gt;</pre>\n</div></div>",
     "created": "15/Nov/18 12:46 PM",
     "id": "20530",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/12824/comment/20530",
